<p>Taught by historian <a href="https://munkschool.utoronto.ca/person/marci-shore">Marci Shore</a>, “<a href="https://online.yale.edu/courses/european-intellectual-history-nietzsche">European Intellectual History Since Nietzsche</a>” surveys the story of modern thought, from the late 18th century to the late 20th.</p>
<p>Along the way, the course explores major trends in modern European thought: Marxism-Leninism, psychoanalysis, expressionism, structuralism, phenomenology, existentialism, anti-politics, and deconstruction. Intellectual figures covered in the course include Nietzsche, Lenin, Kafka, Freud, Husserl, de Beauvoir, Heidegger, Arendt, Adorno, Sartre, Girard, Foucault, Derrida, and Havel.</p>
<p>You can watch all 25 lectures above. Or find them on <a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLh9mgdi4rNezUjm7niGdUWjnL0lHSDh0U">YouTube</a> and <a href="https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/european-intellectual-history-since-nietzsche/id1729418165">Apple Podcasts</a>. Explore <a href="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1xdwxOa5-rvcbdeQsyo-D-x9QV11WGkXd">the course handouts here</a>.</p>
<p>“<a href="https://online.yale.edu/courses/european-intellectual-history-nietzsche">European Intellectual History Since Nietzsche</a>” will be added to our collection, <a href="https://www.openculture.com/freeonlinecourses">1,700 Free Online Courses from Top Universities</a>.</p>
